{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Face to face.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): it is possible to interpret it as flowing on to what follows, joined with 'as a man speaks to his fellow,' so that the sense of the verse is: 'and HaShem spoke to Moses as a man speaks to his fellow, face to face' — that is, without any intermediary between them; so was the speaking of the exalted One with Moses, without intermediary. And this verse explains the superiority of Moses' prophecy, which was without intermediary, unlike the rest of the prophets." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: 'face to face' is an expression of anger. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses: Moses, did I not tell you — when I am angry with them, you are appeased, and when you are angry with them, I am appeased; but now I am angry and you are angry. 'Return to the camp' — do not read it as ושב אל המחנה but as ושוב אל המחנה, in anger: if so, who will draw Israel near? And it says, 'and HaShem spoke to Moses face to face.' Rabbi Yehoshua ben Levi said: we do not know whether the lowly one exalted himself or the exalted One lowered Himself; rather, as it were, the Exalted One of the world bent Himself down, as is said (Exodus 34:5): ״וירד ה' בענן״." "<b>And furthermore</b> they interpreted in Berakhot, in the chapter HaRo'eh: 'and return to the camp' — the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: restore the Tent to the camp, and if not, behold Joshua your minister — 'a youth who did not depart from within the Tent' — from among them, and he will serve in your stead; and despite all this, the matter did not go to waste." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'and HaShem spoke to Moses face to face' — like (Numbers 12:8) ״פה אל פה אדבר בו״, and it is not like (Deuteronomy 5:4) ״פנים בפנים דבר ה' עמכם״, for that was in the attainment of Israel, which was a vision within a vision, in the manner of what is written (Numbers 14:14) ״אשר עין בעין נראה אתה ה'״, and this is clear." "<b>And his minister Joshua son of Nun, a youth.</b> All the days of Joshua were 110 years: 40 years that they journeyed in the wilderness, and 14 years in the Land — 7 years of conquest and 7 of division; if so, he was 56 years old, and how can the verse call him 'a youth'? But the meaning of נער משרת is that the master is called איש and the minister is called נער, and likewise the verse explains (Esther 2:2): ״נערי המלך משרתיו״ — for the word משרתיו is a gloss on נערים."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:47.863135238Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}